WEBVTT

00:09.400 --> 00:11.570
Thanks for helping us out.

00:11.820 --> 00:15.070
No problem. I've always
wanted to wear a miko's outfit.

00:15.070 --> 00:18.620
So these are "shide" streamers?
They're fun to make!

00:18.620 --> 00:21.500
So Kara, your dad is a Shinto priest, huh?

00:21.870 --> 00:24.830
Our family has been taking over
the chief priest role for generations.

00:25.210 --> 00:29.590
I don't know if it's just in my blood,
but I do rather like a shrine's atmosphere.

00:30.750 --> 00:32.340
A torii that stands tall and elegantly.

00:32.970 --> 00:34.680
The sound of trees rustling.

00:35.380 --> 00:38.220
And occasionally, you see...

00:38.220 --> 00:39.600
a cat?

00:39.930 --> 00:40.850
What is this?

00:40.850 --> 00:42.600
- It's magic.
- I hope so!

00:42.930 --> 00:46.980
I cast the spell Ani-snippy on this
shide paper that we've been working on.

00:47.440 --> 00:50.360
Cut it up into a certain creature
and it'll start moving around like it.

00:50.360 --> 00:52.440
"Moving around like it."
You say it so casually!

00:52.440 --> 00:55.030
It's scary!
You made a living creature!

00:56.820 --> 00:58.570
After it moves around for a bit,
it'll disappear.

00:58.570 --> 01:01.740
So you can't give life to a creature
made from magic after all, huh?

01:02.700 --> 01:05.920
Well, if that's the case,
I'm gonna make one, too.

01:05.920 --> 01:07.500
So you're gonna join in after all?

01:07.880 --> 01:09.040
I did it!

01:09.210 --> 01:10.130
Did what?

01:10.540 --> 01:13.710
I-It's a bird, no matter how you
look at it, right? It's gonna fly in the sky!

01:13.710 --> 01:15.470
I thought it was a banana peel.

01:15.470 --> 01:17.340
Kara's kinda clumsy, so...

01:17.340 --> 01:18.800
Let's let it fly!

01:19.390 --> 01:20.850
And, go!

01:31.150 --> 01:32.940
K-Kara, you did it.

01:34.940 --> 01:37.240
You created life!

03:08.500 --> 03:13.080
KARA AND SHIKI

03:08.790 --> 03:10.710
This is a shikigami.

03:11.040 --> 03:13.080
It's also considered
a familiar for onmyouji sorcerers.

03:13.630 --> 03:18.130
It's said that Abe no Seimei used
and controlled various kinds of shikigami.

03:18.510 --> 03:22.130
Its shape resembles the paper dolls
that divine spirits would possess.

03:22.590 --> 03:25.050
So in other words, you wanted
to cut it into a bird shape,

03:25.050 --> 03:28.140
but you were so bad at it
that it turned into a shikigami shape.

03:28.140 --> 03:32.060
It's also weird that it's not disappearing
after moving around so much.

03:32.390 --> 03:37.320
Nico's spell, the shrine's power spot,
and Kara's bloodline.

03:37.440 --> 03:40.400
By these three powers
combining all at once,

03:40.400 --> 03:43.450
something similar to a chemical reaction
might've happened.

03:43.450 --> 03:45.740
So you're saying you don't really get it.

03:46.280 --> 03:48.580
No, don't give me that,
"It's nice to meet you" bow!

03:48.910 --> 03:50.960
Wait, am I going to be taking care of it?

03:50.960 --> 03:52.960
No way. We can't have pets at my place.

03:53.120 --> 03:56.130
But that's so irresponsible of you
when you weren't ready.

03:56.130 --> 03:57.750
It was suddenly born!

03:57.750 --> 04:00.670
Your spell made it, so why don't
you take it to the Otogi house!

04:00.670 --> 04:04.130
Oh hey, that's my time. All right everyone,
good luck with the rest of your day!

04:04.130 --> 04:05.340
See you later, Shiki!

04:05.340 --> 04:09.180
Don't just give it a name.
That'll put more life into it!

04:09.180 --> 04:11.730
Hey, don't run away. Hey!

04:16.270 --> 04:18.190
Oh come on,
don't make this so awkward.

04:19.940 --> 04:24.030
I'm sorry. I honestly don't know
what to do about this, either.

04:25.780 --> 04:28.080
"Oh no, please don't worry about it."

04:28.080 --> 04:29.580
Are you sure you're a piece of paper?

04:29.580 --> 04:31.700
Your behavior is almost too human.

04:32.040 --> 04:33.790
Oh wow, a cute miko.

04:33.790 --> 04:35.790
The ones in 3D aren't bad, either.

04:35.790 --> 04:37.840
Hey, stop taking pictures without asking!

04:38.090 --> 04:39.250
Why you...

04:40.050 --> 04:41.510
What? What is it?

04:46.840 --> 04:48.550
I-It's a monster!

04:48.550 --> 04:51.470
That was amazing.
And you look so proud, too.

04:51.930 --> 04:54.440
I see, shikigami are like familiars.

04:54.440 --> 04:58.480
Just like how Morihito protects Nico,
you're protecting me.

04:59.270 --> 05:01.230
"Aww, it's nothing like that," you say?

05:02.320 --> 05:05.110
You're so full of gestures, Shiki.

05:06.530 --> 05:09.830
<i>And so, this is how Kara
and Shiki's daily life began.</i>

05:10.700 --> 05:13.160
What? You're coming with me
to school, too?

05:13.910 --> 05:16.170
What do shikigamis eat, anyway?

05:16.170 --> 05:18.130
Let's try feeding it some bonito flakes.

05:18.750 --> 05:20.840
He was just asking for directions.

05:21.460 --> 05:23.920
You want to try taking a bath with me?

05:23.920 --> 05:27.590
But you're made from paper, so if you
get wet, you might get torn up and die.

05:29.090 --> 05:30.390
GRADE 1 CLASS 3

05:30.010 --> 05:32.390
Hey. What's with that pose?

05:33.850 --> 05:37.980
Something like, "I'm gonna do it"?
It's so annoying how you emphasize it.

05:38.900 --> 05:40.110
Sheesh.

05:40.110 --> 05:41.770
I'm gonna go take out the trash.

05:42.980 --> 05:45.150
Wait, I accidentally copied you.

05:45.150 --> 05:48.030
Am I some kind of
energetic, happy girl?

05:48.860 --> 05:49.910
Isn't that true, though?

05:51.830 --> 05:54.040
Hey, wait for me.

05:55.500 --> 05:58.000
Come on, stop running.

06:10.680 --> 06:12.600
Hey, what do you think that is?

06:12.600 --> 06:14.010
Something white is floating.

06:14.010 --> 06:15.850
Maybe some kind of cloth?

06:15.850 --> 06:19.560
I guess you stand out a lot
if you're floating around me, huh?

06:19.560 --> 06:22.270
If only you had some kind of spot
that you could perch on.

06:26.280 --> 06:30.820
Huh? My head? "I'll become your hair clip,
so please remove it"?

06:31.320 --> 06:32.700
I'm sorry, Shiki.

06:33.080 --> 06:35.660
I really like this clip a lot,
so I don't want to remove it.

06:37.330 --> 06:39.710
Please don't be all, "I'm gonna do it!"

06:41.080 --> 06:43.340
Hey! I said stop that!

06:48.260 --> 06:51.340
That was my precious keepsake.

06:51.930 --> 06:54.560
My mom bought that hair clip for me!

06:57.730 --> 06:59.810
And there's more water
because of yesterday's rain.

07:02.610 --> 07:04.610
<i>Yes, that's a cute hair clip.</i>

07:14.240 --> 07:15.240
It's fine.

07:16.950 --> 07:18.160
I'll just let it go.

07:31.090 --> 07:33.050
Wait, no! You can't!

07:34.470 --> 07:35.390
Shiki!

07:39.390 --> 07:40.560
Shiki!

07:45.650 --> 07:47.900
Shiki!

08:02.210 --> 08:06.210
Shiki!

08:07.550 --> 08:08.960
You didn't die?

08:10.090 --> 08:12.220
It really seemed like
you were going to die!

08:12.340 --> 08:16.850
In slow motion, you were getting crushed
by the water, and then I thought you died!

08:18.640 --> 08:21.890
That's right, the shide paper
you're made from is meant to be outside,

08:21.890 --> 08:23.560
so you're actually waterproof.

08:25.150 --> 08:26.110
Shiki.

08:30.940 --> 08:36.320
And so, since they almost have the same
shape, my hair clip has become its perch.

08:36.320 --> 08:38.530
Aww, that's so cute.

08:38.530 --> 08:41.000
A hair clip and paper clip in one!

08:40.290 --> 08:42.960
DIVINE HAIR CLIP

08:55.180 --> 08:58.970
I was born and raised
in good ol' Shibamata in Katsushika City.

08:58.970 --> 09:00.970
Kan, you're such a Tora-san otaku.

09:01.140 --> 09:04.850
Yep, Tora-san has been
a big inspiration in my life.

09:01.520 --> 09:06.690
MEGA MARBLE MANIA MADNESS

09:04.850 --> 09:07.650
I feel like you'll make a good salesman.

09:07.650 --> 09:12.940
Heck yeah. With my silver tongue,
I bet I can get you to buy this marble.

09:12.940 --> 09:14.860
Nah, I don't need a marble.

09:15.200 --> 09:16.450
Well, shucks.

09:16.450 --> 09:20.660
Morihito and Miharu are sharp,
and also pretty stingy about their money.

09:20.660 --> 09:23.750
Kan, you're the one who likes
to spend money, and then there's...

09:23.750 --> 09:24.910
Hey.

09:24.910 --> 09:26.370
What're you guys talking about?

09:28.960 --> 09:31.590
All righty, come on down
and take a gander!

09:31.590 --> 09:34.720
What I have here
isn't just a plain old ball of glass.

09:34.720 --> 09:35.930
That's a marble.

09:35.930 --> 09:37.800
Yes, a marble!

09:37.800 --> 09:39.760
When we were all young boys and girls,

09:39.760 --> 09:43.430
we flicked them, hid them in our treasure box,
and turned them into dragon balls.

09:43.430 --> 09:44.890
Yes, the very same marble!

09:44.890 --> 09:48.310
But you'd be wrong if you think
this is some plain old marble!

09:48.310 --> 09:52.020
Why don't we get that handsome face
closer so you can take a good look.

09:52.020 --> 09:53.070
Oh, okay.

09:53.070 --> 09:55.190
Ain't that the prettiest thing
you've ever laid eyes on?

09:55.190 --> 09:56.280
Oh, yeah.

09:56.280 --> 10:01.580
The twisty swirl you see inside
is what industry people call "flame."

09:59.570 --> 10:00.820
THIS IS A LIE

10:01.580 --> 10:05.410
It's normally red or blue, right?
But this one's a rainbow flame!

10:04.830 --> 10:08.580
THESE ARE ALL LIES

10:05.410 --> 10:07.830
And that's actually pretty rare.

10:08.580 --> 10:09.670
Wow!

10:09.670 --> 10:11.040
<i>He believed him.</i>

10:11.040 --> 10:12.090
But wait, there's more!

10:12.090 --> 10:16.840
Air pockets tend to form inside the marble
when it's getting manufactured, but this one...

10:17.130 --> 10:19.050
doesn't have any at all!

10:19.050 --> 10:20.340
That's pretty rare, you know?

10:20.340 --> 10:23.510
With absolutely no impurities,
it's so beautiful and clear.

10:22.760 --> 10:23.850
MANY, MANY LIES

10:25.140 --> 10:26.850
<i>Keigo, aren't you a little too gullible?</i>

10:27.020 --> 10:30.600
You probably can't find a marble with a rainbow
flame and no air bubbles anywhere.

10:30.600 --> 10:32.770
Wow, that's amazing.

10:32.980 --> 10:36.570
And we all know how supply
and demand works, right?

10:36.570 --> 10:38.240
So, something like this
would probably cost...

10:38.240 --> 10:39.860
around 3,000 yen.

10:39.860 --> 10:41.740
Seriously? For just one marble?

10:42.200 --> 10:43.620
But I still want one.

10:43.620 --> 10:44.790
<i>Seriously?</i>

10:44.950 --> 10:48.210
I had no interest at all,
but now I really want one.

10:48.210 --> 10:51.000
Stop it, stop stimulating
my materialistic greed!

10:51.000 --> 10:54.000
Kan, can you please
give that marble to Keigo?

10:54.000 --> 10:56.510
All right, all right. Here, take it.

10:56.670 --> 11:00.090
What? Really?
But it's such a precious thing...

11:00.260 --> 11:02.850
You're a great guy.

11:03.680 --> 11:06.470
What's up guys, it's Keigo.

11:06.970 --> 11:11.230
<i>Oh man, so today,
I'd like to introduce this one item.</i>

11:06.970 --> 11:14.980
[RARE ITEM] SHOWING OFF THIS RARE SPECIMEN
THAT I FINALLY OBTAINED

11:11.230 --> 11:12.940
<i>Check it out!</i>

11:12.940 --> 11:14.980
<i>It looks like a normal marble, right?</i>

11:15.230 --> 11:17.320
<i>But it's actually not.</i>

11:17.320 --> 11:18.860
<i>You see the swirly thing inside?</i>

11:18.860 --> 11:25.120
<i>It's called a flame, and normally
it's red or blue, but the rare ones are...</i>

11:20.490 --> 11:25.120
BUT IT'S JUST A MARBLE
I'VE NEVER HEARD OF THAT, IS THAT TRUE?
WHAT? WHAT IS THIS?
I WANT TO KNOW MORE!

11:26.200 --> 11:29.160
Hey, Magami.
I saw your video about the marble.

11:29.160 --> 11:30.660
O-Oh, hey Rin.

11:30.660 --> 11:33.380
No one really watches my stuff,
so I just post whatever I want, really.

11:33.380 --> 11:36.550
But last I heard, your videos
were pretty popping and going viral, huh?

11:37.300 --> 11:39.470
Nah, my stuff's no big deal.

11:39.470 --> 11:43.260
So I was thinking about introducing
marbles on my channel, too.

11:43.430 --> 11:45.800
Do you think you can teach me about them?

11:49.390 --> 11:53.150
Oh, what? You're interested in marbs?

11:53.850 --> 11:55.360
Rin Fuwa Channel!

11:53.850 --> 11:55.360
RIN FUWA CHANNEL

11:55.560 --> 11:57.610
Hello, cuties! It's Rin-rin.

11:57.610 --> 12:00.860
Today's recommended item
isn't actually makeup.

12:00.860 --> 12:04.370
Ta-da! It's a marble! Clap, clap.

12:04.820 --> 12:07.330
<i>My classmate uploaded
a video about marbles.</i>

12:07.330 --> 12:08.950
<i>Oh, I'll post a link in the description.</i>

12:09.080 --> 12:12.920
<i>Yay, here it is.
Rainbow colors are actually rare.</i>

12:13.330 --> 12:14.040
Wow.

12:14.290 --> 12:15.080
Wow.

12:15.080 --> 12:16.420
Marbles are so cute.

12:16.750 --> 12:18.920
<i>Hello everyone. For today...</i>

12:19.050 --> 12:21.550
Hey there! Today's recommended item is...

12:21.760 --> 12:24.390
Just look at it. Hardly any air bubbles.

12:24.390 --> 12:26.550
- Marbles!
- Flame!

12:26.890 --> 12:29.930
You wanna do a collaboration
with the Kan and Nico's Channel?

12:30.270 --> 12:34.560
Who's gonna watch a collaboration between
two channels that no one watches?

12:34.560 --> 12:37.690
Keigo, that's just called
a "Who's that?" collaboration.

12:37.690 --> 12:41.740
Your passion for online streaming
has seriously gone cold, huh?

12:41.940 --> 12:43.780
There's something I want to do.

12:44.610 --> 12:47.280
It's probably another
"candid camera" kind of video, isn't it?

12:47.280 --> 12:48.990
Those are super cringy, so no way.

12:48.990 --> 12:51.330
You'll get canceled if you're too reckless
with your friends.

12:51.330 --> 12:54.080
You're gonna end up wearing a suit
and having to apologize.

12:54.460 --> 12:57.710
<i>Rainbow flames like this
are actually pretty rare.</i>

12:54.460 --> 12:57.710
[RARE ITEM] SHOWING OFF THIS RARE SPECIMEN
THAT I FINALLY OBTAINED

12:57.710 --> 13:05.090
THUMP THUMP THUMP

12:58.040 --> 12:59.250
Wait, what is this?

12:59.250 --> 13:01.130
You actually posted this?

13:01.130 --> 13:04.470
Yeah, so as a marble specialist,
I'd like you to be in a video with me.

13:05.090 --> 13:06.970
160,000 VIEWS

13:05.380 --> 13:06.970
Look at all those views!

13:07.260 --> 13:09.720
Even the recommended videos
are all marble related!

13:09.720 --> 13:11.810
When did marbles become that popular?

13:11.810 --> 13:13.600
You didn't know?

13:14.060 --> 13:17.560
I made a video
out of the information you gave me,

13:17.560 --> 13:21.070
and from there it went to Rin Fuwa,
and gradually started spreading.

13:19.860 --> 13:21.360
RIN FUWA FOLLOWERS

13:21.480 --> 13:24.950
By now, it's reached
various influencers on social media.

13:26.530 --> 13:29.490
Dang it, all the 100 yen stores
have been picked clean.

13:29.490 --> 13:32.200
Huh? What about the 100 yen stores?

13:32.200 --> 13:34.750
These marbs! Don't you know?

13:32.870 --> 13:34.750
THUMP THUMP THUMP THUMP

13:34.910 --> 13:37.460
They're totally popular
among the junior high kids!

13:37.460 --> 13:39.500
Check these out. Aren't they beautiful?

13:39.500 --> 13:41.090
I'm looking for one called "Inferno,"

13:39.500 --> 13:49.010
THUMP THUMP THUMP THUMP THUMP

13:41.090 --> 13:43.840
which has orange and yellow flames,
and no air bubbles in it.

13:43.840 --> 13:46.880
But marbs with names are rare
so getting one is pretty difficult.

13:46.880 --> 13:49.010
I wonder when they'll get restocked?

13:49.550 --> 13:51.310
Has this gotten a little too out of hand?

13:51.310 --> 13:54.890
Yes it has! There are all these
unknown details and random info, too.

13:55.310 --> 13:57.390
Details... Random info...

13:57.560 --> 13:59.150
Wait, could he also be...

13:59.400 --> 14:01.900
- It's sold out everywhere!
- Oh no, Moi!

14:02.230 --> 14:04.110
What's going on in Japan?

14:04.110 --> 14:06.110
They're all swarming over these marbles.

14:06.110 --> 14:08.110
I have no choice
but to travel really far now!

14:08.860 --> 14:13.490
The Random Info King, the ultimate
Detail Maniac has set his sights on marbles!

14:13.490 --> 14:15.830
Morihito, are you after Inferno as well?

14:15.830 --> 14:20.040
Inferno? Ah, the vitamin-colored flame
that's popular among the junior high kids.

14:20.500 --> 14:22.880
If you're still longing for no air bubbles,

14:22.880 --> 14:25.880
then in the marble mania world,
you're still just a little crumb.

14:26.300 --> 14:28.800
He already thinks
he's an authority figure!

14:28.800 --> 14:32.510
I actually prefer more air bubbles.
I'm a bubbler!

14:32.510 --> 14:33.560
A bubbler?

14:33.560 --> 14:35.980
Plenty of air bubbles, no flame,
and a beautiful blue color.

14:35.980 --> 14:39.730
It's called "Bubble Blue,"
and it's sought after by many fanatics.

14:39.980 --> 14:42.270
Truly a gemstone
that humans gave birth to!

14:42.270 --> 14:44.110
Some kind of value has been created!

14:44.110 --> 14:46.820
If you're after Bubble Blue,
then I have something amazing.

14:47.280 --> 14:50.740
Lapis Lazuli Planet. Definitely a gemstone
that humans gave birth to.

14:50.740 --> 14:51.910
Enough already!

14:51.910 --> 14:54.910
Please sell that to me, Keigo.
We're friends, right?

14:54.910 --> 14:59.960
Keigo, do you have a gun ball of Inferno?
I'll trade you my Fairy World for it.

14:59.960 --> 15:02.210
Stop it, everyone.
I can't listen to this anymore.

15:02.540 --> 15:05.590
It's no use! Everyone's eyes look like
the black flame of a marble.

15:05.800 --> 15:07.300
Listen, all of you.

15:08.760 --> 15:10.220
The... The thing is...

15:10.220 --> 15:12.050
Why are you crying?

15:12.470 --> 15:13.930
You idiot!

15:14.050 --> 15:15.430
What're we gonna do about this?

15:15.430 --> 15:17.640
It's already spread far too wide
to tell people it was a lie.

15:17.640 --> 15:18.980
Did you cast a spell, Nico?

15:18.980 --> 15:20.440
Th-The thing is...

15:20.690 --> 15:22.650
I didn't cast a spell.

15:22.650 --> 15:26.690
I was only having fun.
I didn't mean to let it go this far.

15:26.690 --> 15:28.070
It's social media.

15:29.030 --> 15:31.990
It gives birth to trends with an explosive
power to spread them far and wide.

15:31.990 --> 15:35.410
The promotional effect that influencers
have is especially exceptional!

15:35.410 --> 15:38.200
That's what the current magic is
in this world.

15:38.540 --> 15:41.960
Wasn't this person
just calling marbles gemstones?

15:41.960 --> 15:43.580
Moi, what should we do?

15:43.880 --> 15:46.090
Don't worry.
I'm sure the craze will end soon.

15:47.380 --> 15:51.590
Look at the marbles being posted with high prices
on free market apps and auction websites.

15:51.970 --> 15:53.300
No one's buying them, right?

15:53.300 --> 15:54.760
You're right.

15:54.760 --> 15:57.430
If there are no buyers,
then the prices will drop.

15:57.430 --> 15:58.930
That's great!

15:58.930 --> 16:00.520
Hey, you're right.

16:00.520 --> 16:03.100
Looks like the craze
is quickly heading toward its end.

16:03.100 --> 16:04.270
You can tell?

16:04.270 --> 16:07.320
Keigo's channel is getting attacked.

16:07.320 --> 16:08.780
What?!

16:09.820 --> 16:12.200
<i>What's up guys, it's Keigo.</i>

16:12.200 --> 16:15.240
<i>So, um, this is an emergency video.</i>

16:15.240 --> 16:17.540
<i>I posted a video on this channel
relating to marbles,</i>

16:17.540 --> 16:21.160
<i>and I've discovered that some
of the information was not actually true.</i>

16:21.580 --> 16:22.870
<i>I'm really...</i>

16:22.870 --> 16:39.140
[APOLOGY] CONFESSING ALL
REGARDING THE MARBLE INCIDENT

16:23.170 --> 16:24.960
<i>terribly sorry about all this.</i>

16:25.330 --> 16:28.840
<i>And so, um, the friends who told me
about that information</i>

16:28.840 --> 16:32.380
<i>are also here,
and they would like to apologize as well.</i>

16:32.380 --> 16:33.550
<i>Okay, this way please.</i>

16:36.430 --> 16:39.140
<i>- I'm Kanshi from Kan and Nico's Channel.
- I'm Nico.</i>

16:39.600 --> 16:42.100
<i>We are very sorry
for what has happened.</i>

16:42.100 --> 16:44.560
A prank went too far, and we had
to dress in suits and apologize.

16:44.560 --> 16:46.900
We even did a "Who's that?" collaboration.

16:49.020 --> 16:50.440
Hup.

16:50.440 --> 16:51.900
What's this box?

16:50.440 --> 16:57.370
SCRAMBLE SCRAP SQUAD

16:51.900 --> 16:55.490
I was organizing the shed
and found some things from my past.

16:55.820 --> 16:58.280
It's stuff I made
when I was in elementary school.

16:58.620 --> 17:01.040
Drawings, calligraphy, there's even a haiku.

17:01.040 --> 17:03.830
You saved things like this?
You're so diligent.

17:04.920 --> 17:06.000
What's this?

17:06.000 --> 17:07.170
No, don't look at that.

17:07.290 --> 17:08.920
What is it?
I bet it's something perverted.

17:08.920 --> 17:11.130
Maybe it's a crappy manga that
you drew when you were a kid.

17:11.130 --> 17:12.720
Maybe a love letter?

17:12.720 --> 17:14.430
What are you hiding?

17:14.430 --> 17:17.930
FIGHT! MARTIAL WARRIORS
BATTLE FIGHTERS

17:15.130 --> 17:17.930
It was a crappy manga
that you drew when you were a kid!

17:18.430 --> 17:21.310
Yeah, there was a time when
I was obsessed with drawing it.

17:22.140 --> 17:25.140
One chapter had ten pages, and I drew
72 chapters. I never showed it to anyone.

17:25.140 --> 17:26.440
What kind of dedication is that?

17:26.810 --> 17:28.520
It's embarrassing, so don't read it!

17:28.520 --> 17:31.190
Just a little bit!
What do we have here?

17:31.190 --> 17:36.700
FIGHT! MARTIAL WARRIORS
BATTLE FIGHTERS

17:31.480 --> 17:34.530
"Fight! Martial Warriors Battle Fighters!"

17:34.780 --> 17:36.700
- The pressure to fight is strong.
- Don't read it.

17:36.780 --> 17:38.950
The drawings and dialogue are super cute.

17:38.950 --> 17:40.280
Please don't read it.

17:40.450 --> 17:43.660
The Southern Cross combo attack they
used in the Bad Man fight is amazing!

17:43.660 --> 17:45.540
The action in the first half
is pretty effective.

17:45.540 --> 17:47.420
The morals behind
"Monchak" are pretty out there.

17:47.670 --> 17:49.250
How far are you reading?

17:49.250 --> 17:52.960
But I think it's pretty good.
The drawings suck though.

17:52.960 --> 17:55.760
As a kid, I was pretty obsessed
with drawing it.

17:56.090 --> 17:59.430
At the time, I really wanted
to be in that world.

17:59.640 --> 18:00.640
I got it!

18:00.640 --> 18:02.810
There's a spell that will
make your dreams come true.

18:03.020 --> 18:06.190
Wait, what do you mean?
Like we can go into this manga's world?

18:06.190 --> 18:08.730
- Yes, or rather...
- That's a great idea!

18:08.730 --> 18:10.730
- It sounds fun!
- Take me there!

18:10.730 --> 18:13.230
Oh no, the boys really want to go
into this manga's world.

18:13.570 --> 18:15.650
Okay, I'm gonna cast the spell,
so please line up.

18:15.650 --> 18:16.950
Is this one of the safe ones?

18:16.950 --> 18:18.610
Gra-pic!

18:23.660 --> 18:26.290
Sheesh, your front door was unlocked.

18:26.290 --> 18:28.790
I was in the area,
so I wanted to stop by.

18:29.790 --> 18:32.880
What? Picture? What?

18:32.880 --> 18:34.210
Oh, hi Kara.

18:34.460 --> 18:36.420
Wh-What's going on?

18:36.720 --> 18:39.430
- I cast a spell.
- Yeah, I bet!

18:39.550 --> 18:43.100
Everyone looks like
a crappy drawing that a kid drew.

18:43.470 --> 18:45.180
Crappy? No it's not!

18:45.180 --> 18:46.850
He sounds like a kid, too.

18:47.060 --> 18:51.150
We wanted to go into the manga
that Morihito drew when he was a kid, but...

18:51.150 --> 18:55.110
...the spell turned us
into the manga drawing itself.

18:55.230 --> 18:58.360
You guys are just living daily life
on the edge as usual, huh?

18:58.490 --> 19:00.410
Wait, where's Kanshi?

19:00.410 --> 19:01.370
I'm right here.

19:01.990 --> 19:06.660
Why am I the only one who has a woodblock
print specialist's edgy and rough depiction?

19:06.660 --> 19:07.960
No!

19:08.040 --> 19:09.710
Scary! The art style is way too strong!

19:09.710 --> 19:10.830
Don't run from me!

19:11.130 --> 19:15.840
Looks like Kan took on the woodblock print
that was mixed in with the manga.

19:16.010 --> 19:19.550
I called it "Angry Friend,"
and I won first place with it.

19:19.840 --> 19:21.550
The etchings are pretty strong.

19:21.720 --> 19:24.390
Don't sing your own praises
when I'm like this!

19:26.970 --> 19:29.640
Huh? A piece of paper flew away.

19:30.520 --> 19:33.480
That's called, "Fight!
Martial Warriors Battle Fighters!"

19:33.480 --> 19:34.360
What now?

19:34.360 --> 19:38.690
It's the page I used to cast the spell.
We won't be able to turn back if we lose it.

19:38.690 --> 19:39.780
What?

19:39.780 --> 19:41.360
That's not good.

19:41.360 --> 19:42.530
What should we do?

19:42.530 --> 19:44.030
We gotta think of something.

19:44.370 --> 19:47.040
It's like I'm reading a comedy manga
with no tension.

19:47.290 --> 19:50.580
Okay, it's come down to this.
Let's go! It's time to...

19:48.500 --> 19:50.580
RUMBLE RUMBLE

19:52.120 --> 19:53.540
Scramble!

19:53.540 --> 19:54.790
Now wait just a darn minute.

19:54.960 --> 19:58.090
You already look super suspicious already,
so please don't Scramble like that.

19:58.460 --> 20:00.510
Don't forget about me.

20:00.930 --> 20:01.760
The woodblock?

20:01.760 --> 20:05.350
I can turn back to normal!
Get me back to normal first!

20:05.680 --> 20:08.430
Kanshi's anger is really matching
with the woodblock's art.

20:08.430 --> 20:11.310
Ugh, stop squirming around so much,
you little rough drafts!

20:11.520 --> 20:14.310
It looks like I've become
the magic user now.

20:15.520 --> 20:17.820
Shoot, someone's coming! Everyone, hide.

20:17.820 --> 20:19.610
But there's no where to hide.

20:17.820 --> 20:21.700
PANIC PANIC PANIC

20:19.610 --> 20:21.700
Oh no, we're done for!

20:25.830 --> 20:26.700
Wall art!

20:28.290 --> 20:30.250
We're putting our 2D characteristics
to good use.

20:30.250 --> 20:32.370
No, you were the one
who stood out the most.

20:32.540 --> 20:34.080
Let's just hurry up and look for it.

20:34.080 --> 20:36.500
Based on the wind, it's this direction.

20:36.500 --> 20:38.130
I hope we find it soon.

20:38.380 --> 20:40.460
I know! Leave this to me!

20:42.630 --> 20:43.470
Rawr!

20:43.470 --> 20:45.510
Yeah, they're just really cute.

20:46.050 --> 20:48.260
I smell it over there!

20:48.430 --> 20:49.930
It's being held there by the wind.

20:49.930 --> 20:52.060
Let's hurry and grab it
before it gets blown away again.

20:52.060 --> 20:53.480
Let's grab it while we can.

20:53.480 --> 20:54.730
Wait.

20:54.730 --> 20:56.900
There's something weird
happening inside the room.

20:57.230 --> 20:58.900
- A thief!
- A bad guy?

20:59.070 --> 21:00.650
Okay, let's go! Hyah!

21:00.900 --> 21:01.940
Right!

21:04.240 --> 21:05.490
This is it!

21:06.120 --> 21:08.780
Merge! Southern Cross!

21:08.990 --> 21:11.200
Get 'em!

21:18.670 --> 21:20.210
What? Wh-What?

21:22.090 --> 21:23.670
You're okay now.

21:23.880 --> 21:25.050
Don't get in my way!

21:25.300 --> 21:29.310
We're gonna punch the bad guy!

21:31.180 --> 21:32.930
We did it!

21:34.810 --> 21:38.020
Good job, Martial Warriors Battle Fighters.

21:39.480 --> 21:40.730
We're finally back to normal.

21:40.730 --> 21:42.320
My body feels heavy.

21:42.320 --> 21:43.900
I'm sorry everyone.

21:43.900 --> 21:47.360
Well, we got to defeat a bad guy,
so it turned out all right in the end.

21:47.360 --> 21:49.700
Yeah, and my dream really did come true.

21:50.740 --> 21:53.580
I remembered why I even started
drawing a manga.

21:53.950 --> 21:55.540
When I was a kid...

21:56.170 --> 21:58.000
I didn't have any friends.

21:58.960 --> 22:01.670
Working together with your friends
and taking down the enemy.

22:01.840 --> 22:05.170
And an attack that I could only
dream about actually happened.

22:02.460 --> 22:05.470
SOUTHERN CROSS

22:09.300 --> 22:11.310
Let's think of different moves, too.

22:11.310 --> 22:12.680
We won't need those, right?

22:12.680 --> 22:14.730
I wanted to be part of the merge, too.

22:14.730 --> 22:16.600
Let's add in my transformation, too.

22:16.600 --> 22:20.770
Can you guys please talk about
more normal high school stuff?

22:22.980 --> 22:25.240
Don't forget about me!

22:25.240 --> 22:26.990
FIRST PLACE
"ANGRY FRIEND"
BY MORIHITO OTOGI

23:57.620 --> 24:00.500
Morihito goes alone
to visit his mother's grave.

24:00.500 --> 24:03.080
Standing in front of it, he recalls the bond
he had with young Nico,

24:03.080 --> 24:04.540
and also some special memories.

24:04.540 --> 24:07.250
Meanwhile, at the Otogi house,
Nemu realizes a secret.

24:06.710 --> 24:11.970
NEXT EPISODE
LETTER FROM A FRIEND

24:07.250 --> 24:08.630
Next episode, "Letter From a Friend."

24:08.630 --> 24:11.970
Okay, after this,
we've got more service coming up!
